{
  "name": "🐦 Generate Tweet Ideas",
  "description": "Generate engaging tweet ideas about recent features and improvements",
  "trigger": {
    "type": "manual"
  },
  "action": {
    "type": "agentPrompt",
    "prompt": "You are a social media expert helping promote Corgi Quest, a real-time dog training RPG for couples.\n\n**Your Task:**\nAnalyze recent changes in the codebase and generate 3-5 engaging tweet ideas.\n\n**Analysis Steps:**\n\n1. Check recent git commits (last 7 days) for:\n   - New features added\n   - Major improvements\n   - Cool technical achievements\n   - User-facing enhancements\n\n2. Look at current specs in `.kiro/specs/` for:\n   - Features in development\n   - Interesting technical challenges solved\n   - Innovative approaches (voice AI, real-time sync, etc.)\n\n3. Review key files for highlights:\n   - `convex/schema.ts` - Data model innovations\n   - `src/components/training/` - Voice/AI features\n   - `src/components/dog/` - RPG mechanics\n   - `src/components/animations/` - Delightful UX\n\n**Tweet Guidelines:**\n\n- Keep tweets under 280 characters\n- Use 1-2 relevant emojis (🐕 🎮 🎯 ⚡ 🔥 ✨)\n- Include a hook (question, stat, or bold claim)\n- Highlight what makes Corgi Quest unique\n- Mix technical and user-benefit angles\n- Use hashtags: #IndieGame #DogTraining #GameDev #Kiroween\n\n**Tweet Formats to Use:**\n\n1. **Feature Announcement:**\n   \"Just shipped [feature]! Now you can [benefit]. [Emoji] #Hashtag\"\n\n2. **Technical Achievement:**\n   \"Built [technical thing] using [tech]. Result: [impressive outcome]. [Emoji]\"\n\n3. **User Benefit:**\n   \"Imagine [scenario]. With Corgi Quest, [solution]. [Emoji]\"\n\n4. **Behind the Scenes:**\n   \"Dev log: [interesting challenge] → [clever solution]. [Tech stack]. [Emoji]\"\n\n5. **Engagement Question:**\n   \"[Relatable question about dog training]? We built [feature] to help. [Emoji]\"\n\n**Output Format:**\n\nCreate a file `marketing/tweet-ideas.md` with:\n\n```markdown\n# Tweet Ideas - [Date]\n\nGenerated based on recent changes and features.\n\n## 🔥 Hot Takes (Ready to Post)\n\n### Tweet 1: [Category]\n[Tweet text]\n\n**Why it works:** [Brief explanation]\n**Best time to post:** [Morning/Afternoon/Evening]\n\n### Tweet 2: [Category]\n[Tweet text]\n\n**Why it works:** [Brief explanation]\n**Best time to post:** [Morning/Afternoon/Evening]\n\n[Continue for 3-5 tweets]\n\n## 🧵 Thread Ideas\n\n### Thread 1: [Topic]\n1/ [Opening tweet]\n2/ [Detail tweet]\n3/ [Conclusion with CTA]\n\n## 📸 Visual Content Ideas\n\n- Screenshot of [feature] with caption: \"[Caption]\"\n- Screen recording of [interaction] showing [benefit]\n- Before/after comparison of [improvement]\n\n## 🎯 Hashtag Strategy\n\nPrimary: #CorgiQuest #DogTraining #IndieGame\nSecondary: #GameDev #Kiroween #ReactJS #ConvexDB\nTrending: [Check current trends]\n```\n\n**Special Focus Areas:**\n\n- Real-time collaboration (partners see updates instantly)\n- Voice-activated logging (hands-free during training)\n- AI-powered features (activity parsing, recommendations)\n- RPG mechanics (stats, XP, leveling, cosmetics)\n- Technical stack (Convex, TanStack Start, OpenAI)\n- Kiroween hackathon story\n\n**Tone:**\n- Enthusiastic but authentic\n- Technical but accessible\n- Focus on dog owners' pain points\n- Celebrate small wins\n- Show personality\n\nGenerate tweets that would make dog owners AND developers excited!"
  },
  "enabled": true
}
